From: James Halgren <james.halgren@byu.edu>
Date: Fri, 9 Oct 2026 13:19:10 -0600
Subject: [PATCH 04/10] fix(kernel): decide whether to route from the inputs,
 not the intent(out) qdc

The "only solve if there's water to flux" test reads qdc, which is an
intent(out) dummy and is assigned only later. Its value on entry is undefined.
Through T-Route's bind(c) wrapper it is the 0.0 that reach.pyx stores before
the call, so the term never changes a T-Route result. From a Fortran caller
gfortran 15 at -O2 drops the caller's store (intent(out) clobber), and the test
then reads the previous call's outflow: a dry channel (all inflows 0) takes the
flow branch and publishes a non-zero depth and velocity. In a 46,128-case
kernel sweep with qdc = 1 on entry, 3,290 dry cases took the flow branch
(see the PR description).

WRF-Hydro's SUBMUSKINGCUNGE tests ql, qup and qdp; the term qdc > 0 came in
with NOAA-OWP/t-route#111 (2020-09-23). quc stays: T-Route routes current-step
upstream inflow when assume_short_ts is False.

No change to T-Route results (bitwise, all test cases).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 src/kernel/muskingum/MCsingleSegStime_f2py_NOLOOP.f90 | 5 ++++-
 1 file changed, 4 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/src/kernel/muskingum/MCsingleSegStime_f2py_NOLOOP.f90 b/src/kernel/muskingum/MCsingleSegStime_f2py_NOLOOP.f90
index 22af4bd..6299fe7 100644
--- a/src/kernel/muskingum/MCsingleSegStime_f2py_NOLOOP.f90
+++ b/src/kernel/muskingum/MCsingleSegStime_f2py_NOLOOP.f90
@@ -71,8 +71,11 @@ subroutine muskingcungenwm(dt, qup, quc, qdp, ql, dx, bw, tw, twcc,&
     h     = (depthc * 1.33_prec) + mindepth !1.50 of  depthc
     h_0   = (depthc * 0.67_prec)            !0.50 of depthc
 
+    !* Decide from the inputs only. qdc is intent(out): its value on entry is
+    !* undefined (the bind(c) caller passes 0.0; a Fortran caller may pass the
+    !* previous call's result, or nothing at all once the compiler drops the store).
     if(ql .gt. 0.0_prec .or. qup .gt. 0.0_prec .or. quc .gt. 0.0_prec &
-        .or. qdp .gt. 0.0_prec .or. qdc .gt. 0.0_prec) then  !only solve if there's water to flux
+        .or. qdp .gt. 0.0_prec) then  !only solve if there's water to flux
 110 continue
 
         !* Qj_0 = 0 is the reference's (MUSKINGCUNGE.f90 label 110), lost in the
